-- title:
--   Bounding the enveloped complete support series in one carry cell
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ne0$, $k\ge2$, and $R\ge2$, and fix a smooth sieve cutoff $\chi$, selected CFZ pattern $e$, and natural parameters $w,b$. Assume $w$ bounds the exceptional primes of the full CFZ affine-form family and $\operatorname{primorial}(w)$ is coprime to $b$. For every integer carry vector and every paired Fourier coordinate, the norm of the paired cutoff envelope times the complete prime-support series is bounded by the selected complete-support mass times the paired absolute Fourier density.
